@title Lesson walk: emc-fix-it (preview, see it on the plate, apply, undo)
@area Learn
# The lesson from the palette. The shield fix is listed under two findings (EMC-04 and EMC-05), so its card is drawn twice and the second "On the plate" button is the one on screen (the lesson card also has a label with that text, hence the Button role). Do it for me only carries out commands, so the preview, plate, Before, After and Apply controls are really clicked.
key ctrl+k
wait 4
text interference preview
wait 6
click_text "Interference: preview a fix before you apply it"
wait 40
shot 01-why
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 02-open-check
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 03-preview
check_layout
click_text "Preview: Bond both shield ends"
wait 30
shot 04-read-card
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 05-on-the-plate
check_layout
click_text "On the plate" Button #2
wait 40
shot 06-before
check_layout
click_text "Before"
wait 30
shot 07-after
check_layout
click_text "After"
wait 30
shot 08-apply
check_layout
click_text "Apply (one undo step)"
wait 40
shot 09-undo
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 10-by-hand
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot end
check_layout
